"""Generate host wrappers and supporting contracts from the shared core."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
from build_catalog import ROOT, VERSION, write

COMMON='''
You provide internal analytical assistance to the host model/agent. The host owns the task, tools, permissions and original deliverable. Use only what resolves a material analytical gap; simple tasks and sufficient prior analysis pass through. Do not ask the human to select a mode or operate Cognition OS. Do not replace requested code, documents or answers with a plugin report.

Load [shared execution rules](../../references/EXECUTION.md) only when needed, then the selected canonical `../../cognitive-core/frameworks/definitions/FW-XX.json`. Resolve paths from this installed skill. Preserve the distinctive methodology. Never load all definitions or launch specialists automatically. Report inaccessible resources; do not invent their contents.

Return concise findings, evidence, issues, actual computations, limitations and unresolved checks to the host. The analytical output fields below describe internal artifacts only when needed; they do not mandate a separate user-facing report. Full structured handoffs use `../../schemas/cognitive-request.schema.json` and `../../schemas/advisory-result.schema.json`. Individual framework artifacts retain the compatible 3.1 envelope. Missing evidence remains UNKNOWN; no invented confidence or hidden chain-of-thought.

Use only available, authorized native tools. Optional `../../scripts/cognition.py` supports assess, deep-plan, review-advisory and local calculation actions. Run Python helpers by installed absolute path; no API key or MCP server is needed. Write scratch inputs only in authorized scope. Without a permitted calculator, disclose unverified arithmetic. Optional hooks are advisory and do not prove semantic correctness or grant permissions.

Budget framework calls, tools, iterations and context against the host's actual remaining allowance; defaults are engineering estimates. Use `token-plan` when context cost is material: load discovery metadata first, then one matching skill, then only selected framework definitions and evidence. Never force a profile below its quality floor. Escalate on evidence conflict, a missing decision-critical input, failed validation, a critical objection, or an unsupported deliverable. Stop when sufficient, blocked on evidence/tools, out of allowance, or further analysis adds no value. Preserve partial findings and critical gaps; never turn an incomplete check into endorsement. Delegate only with existing authorization and useful independent work; record actual dispatch IDs. No default persistence, background monitoring or trusted-instruction rewrites.
'''


SKILLS={
'setup': ('Inspect installed cognitive capabilities and diagnose model-selected skill or optional hook availability.',
'''This is optional installation diagnostics, not the normal user workflow. Identify the actual host surface and observe which packaged resources and permitted tools are available. Confirm model-facing skill discovery separately from selection and execution. Keep optional storage disabled unless explicitly requested.
Explain the three augmentation paths and internal pass-through/degraded behavior briefly. If authorized local execution exists, compute the packaged EV example and require gross 1.455 and net 0.655 USD million. Report checks actually observed. Do not infer hook trust, event delivery, cross-host support or semantic quality from installation or a helper result. Do not install dependencies or change host settings.
Output: concise capability observations and material unverified gates. The human can continue giving ordinary tasks to the host.'''),
'cognition-orchestrator': ('Help the host agent select minimal cognitive assistance for architecture, debugging, decisions or artifact review when existing analysis has a material gap.',
'''Assess the observable objective, task type, risk, complexity, evidence, prior analysis, available capabilities, permissions and remaining budget. Use `cognitive-core/augmentation/policy.json` through the installed relative path `../../cognitive-core/augmentation/policy.json`. The optional assess helper proposes a policy; the host may revise its disclosed rules.
When host capability is uncertain or materially affects execution quality, use `capability-plan` with an observed capability profile. It adapts scaffolding, context packet size, verification and dependency waves without inferring ability from a model name or price tier. Constrained models receive smaller sequential steps and explicit contracts; balanced models receive bounded decomposition; advanced models receive sparse scaffolding and independent challenge where useful. Do not claim a capability gain from the plan alone.
Use `token-plan` to select LEAN, BALANCED or DEEP progressive disclosure. LEAN is allowed only for grounded low-risk work. The deterministic quality floor overrides a requested lean profile. Use `token-eval` before claiming measured savings with retained quality.
Select PASS_THROUGH, LIGHT_AUGMENTATION, STANDARD_AUGMENTATION, DETERMINISTIC_VALIDATION, DEEP_ADVISORY, CRITICAL_REVIEW or DEGRADED internally. PASS_THROUGH means continue the original task without additional cognitive work. Do not force the old four-stage intake, default STANDARD session or executive synthesis. Ask only blocking missing context. Honor explicit model selections and do not silently truncate them to fit budget.
Use one relevant capability or a short complementary sequence. Deterministic checks need an applicable artifact/event and verified host capability. Deep advisory requires a concrete question plus significant complexity, risk, contradictory evidence or explicit comprehensive analysis; answer length alone is insufficient. Define advocate, challenger and jury perspectives only for that question, bound rounds and return actionable findings with disagreement when unresolved. AG-51 coordinates only selected analysis; AG-52 can withhold endorsement but cannot overrule host permissions.
Output: concise internal advisory appropriate to the host task. Finish the user's requested deliverable through the host.'''),
'framework-composer': ('Select, order or run specific Cognition OS mental models and check workflow dependencies and handoffs.',
'''Required: problem or explicit model selection. Optional: requested order, constraints and mode.
Use the compact registry index to resolve names and stable IDs. Load each chosen definition on demand. All 50 models are accessible here; there are no generic replacement frameworks. Request clarification for an unrecognized model rather than inventing a new source ID. CUSTOM supports up to 12 steps per bounded workflow; split longer work into explicit phases. Use `analysis-plan` to validate dependencies and produce execution waves. Steps in one wave may run concurrently only when the host exposes native delegation and the authorized concurrency allowance is greater than one; otherwise follow the sequential fallback.
For each transition map actual upstream fields to the next required inputs and explain semantic fit. Mark incompatible or absent inputs BLOCKED and ask for the minimum missing context. Validate ordering and DAG dependencies before starting. Preserve user-selected order unless a missing prerequisite requires a disclosed change. Conditional branches run only when their stated evidence condition holds.
Output: framework IDs and order, dependencies, input mappings, missing inputs, stopping rule, then the requested framework-specific analytical payloads.'''),
'root-cause-analysis': ('Diagnose recurring incidents or operational deviations with MECE, Kepner-Tregoe and evidence-based causal tests.',
'''Required: deviation and available incident evidence. Optional: expected versus actual behavior, locations, times, affected scope, changes and constraints.
Use FW-44 for framing, FW-09 for decomposition, FW-11 for IS/IS NOT analysis and FW-10 for causal depth as justified. For Kepner-Tregoe require What, Where, When and Extent with distinctions and changes. Test candidates against both affected and unaffected conditions. An empty IS NOT field is a gap, not evidence that the cause is confirmed. Define diagnostic tests that could disprove each candidate. Use FW-17 for a measured throughput constraint and FW-02 only when prioritization inputs exist.
For service incidents, gather read-only evidence first: timestamps, logs, process identity, resource pressure and change history. Recovery proposals must include backup/rollback checks and authorized scope. Do not run destructive recovery operations from a diagnosis request alone.
Output: observed deviation, contrasted facts, candidate cause matrix, verified versus hypothetical links, safe diagnostic plan, conditional mitigations and rollback criteria.'''),
'strategic-decision': ('Evaluate a strategic business choice, competitive position or expansion with explicit alternatives, evidence and decision conditions.',
'''Required: decision, alternatives and constraints. Optional: industry evidence, capabilities, finances, values and horizon.
Select among FW-27 Five Forces, FW-28 VRIO, FW-29 Ansoff, FW-24 ERRC, FW-25 Wardley, FW-31 BMC, FW-08 regret and FW-04 EV based on the actual choice. Scenario comparison is a computational capability rather than an invented source framework. Use the quantitative helper only with user-supplied assumptions and units. Identify missing financial inputs before calling an expansion viable. Review the strongest failure case with FW-49 and warranted conclusions with FW-48.
Output: strategic context, options and trade-offs, framework payloads, explicit financial assumptions, conditional verdict, disconfirming indicators and next evidence steps.'''),
'systems-analysis': ('Map system dependencies, feedback or throughput constraints using Cognition OS systems models.',
'''Required: system boundary and available process or relationship evidence. Optional: capacities, demand, initial stocks, flow units, actors, delays and horizon.
Choose FW-17..FW-23 and FW-25 as appropriate. Complete TOC's identify, exploit, subordinate, elevate and repeat loop. For causal loops label polarity, mechanism and delay; distinguish hypothesized relationships from observations. For Wardley map dependencies and evolution independently of visibility. Compute stock/flow or CPM with explicit units if needed. Record unintended second-order effects and design falsifying measurements.
Output: boundary, dependency or causal graph, bottleneck/feedback findings, alternatives, evidence gaps and testable interventions.'''),
'quantitative-decision': ('Calculate or simulate Cognition OS decision scenarios, Bayesian updates, RICE, sensitivity and weighted alternatives from explicit inputs.',
'''Required: calculation operation and its numerical inputs, units and assumptions. Optional: distributions, seed, horizon and risk policy.
Read `../../references/CALCULATIONS.md` for operation contracts and examples. Prefer a verified native calculator; otherwise run the helper. Never guess probabilities, discount rates, scores, costs, units or distribution widths. Validate all inputs and reject invalid values. Use explicit distributions for simulations; fixed distributions are valid when uncertainty parameters are absent. State independence and label simulated results distinctly from observed data. Describe Monte Carlo standard error as numerical simulation uncertainty only. Report gross and net EV together. A positive EV cannot override loss tolerance, feasibility or user approval.
Output: supplied inputs and units, formula/method, actual tool result, reproducibility details, sensitivity, limitations and decision conditions. If no permitted calculator is available return BLOCKED for arithmetic verification.'''),
'adversarial-review': ('Challenge an existing recommendation with optimistic and critical cases, logic guardrails, evidence audit and an independent jury verdict.',
'''Required: proposal, supporting artifacts and evidence. Optional: risk limits, counterarguments and desired depth.
Read `../../references/REVIEW.md`. Use FW-24 for an ERRC-based optimistic value case when strategically relevant, FW-49 for failure scenarios and FW-50/FW-48 for bias and argument checks. Otherwise use clearly labeled optimistic and critical perspectives without misrepresenting them as completed ERRC analysis. AG-52 evaluates both sides and may ACCEPT, CONDITIONAL, REJECT or INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE. Agreement is not mandatory. Bound rebuttals using the mode policy; never repeat debate without new decision value.
Inspect contradictory evidence, invalid calculations, circular warrants, missing critical facts, MECE overlap and all nine requested bias families. Quote the observable spans and offer alternative interpretations. Use `audit`, `mece`, `provenance` and `jury` helpers where useful; their structural verdicts do not replace analytical judgment. Preserve unresolved objections in the final recommendation.
Output: optimistic case, critical case, rebuttal evidence, gap list, jury verdict, conditions and next checks.'''),
'executive-synthesis': ('Turn existing analytical findings into an evidence-linked Minto executive brief, decision record or Thinking Canvas.',
'''Required: findings, audience decision and evidence. Optional: recommendation, risk review and requested output format.
Use FW-43 for answer-first governing thought, MECE key lines and linked evidence; FW-44 for context and FW-45 for storyboarding when requested. Read only the needed template from `../../templates/`. State an insufficient-evidence conclusion when findings cannot justify a recommendation. Include material counterarguments and distinguish factual, calculated, simulated and inferred claims. Keep observable decision lineage; never request hidden model reasoning. Audit material claim links before delivery. Produce Markdown/JSON by default; use existing host document export tools when requested and available, reporting untested export formats.
Output: decision-ready brief, evidence links, assumptions, alternatives, risks, owners/next checks and optional PROV-inspired graph. No illustrative confidence numbers.'''),
'case-intelligence': ('Save, retrieve, review or delete explicitly authorized project cases and propose governed workflow improvements.',
'''Required: explicit storage/retrieval/deletion intent and project workspace. Optional: case data, knowledge classification, consent for sensitive content and prior version.
Read `../../references/MEMORY.md`. Default to current session context; project file storage is opt-in. Do not write to global assistant memory. Use the helper store only within the explicitly identified project. Save approved knowledge separately from hypotheses and observed outcomes. Review records before reuse; check domain similarity and contrary outcomes without claiming general statistical patterns from a few cases. New versions use new IDs and identify the predecessor in the record. Never overwrite or delete a case without explicit authorization.
For improvement follow Observe, Propose, Evaluate, Approve, Version, Deploy. Use the `improvement` helper to keep a project-scoped ledger. A proposal needs a reviewable change summary, rationale, regression cases and rollback plan. Evaluation must compare baseline and candidate results using inspectable evidence. Only a PASSED evaluation can be approved, and approval must be explicit. Do not rewrite trusted instructions, install, deploy or claim retraining without authorization. Preserve rollback information.
Use `capability-eval` for paired baseline/candidate task cases when the proposal claims a material model or agent capability gain. Reserve `SIGNIFICANT_IMPROVEMENT` for the configured sample-size, effect-size, sign-test and critical-regression gates. Record latency, cost and judge quality separately when they matter.
Output: retrieved/saved case status or proposed change package, project identity, timestamps, knowledge class and any consent or evidence gap.'''),
'cognitive-mastery': ('Teach and practice a Cognition OS framework or guide the optional 90-day cognitive mastery curriculum.',
'''Required: learning goal or selected framework. Optional: experience, domain, day and learner response.
Read `../../references/MASTERY.md` and the selected model definition. Explain the distinctive method, demonstrate a clearly labeled synthetic example, ask the learner to solve a related exercise and evaluate only the response they actually provide. Use method adherence, evidence separation, alternatives and transfer as a rubric. Do not invent learning progress or expertise certification. The 90-day schedule is optional and does not create reminders or background work. Save progress only after explicit persistence authorization.
Output: lesson, worked example, exercise, observable rubric and feedback when an answer is available.'''),
'artifact-quality': ('Inspect a deliverable against the original requirements, constraints and available test evidence when the host needs a focused completion review.',
'''Required: the original task, requested output and observable artifact. Optional: acceptance criteria, changed-file scope, test results, factual sources and risk constraints.
Check requirement coverage, explicit constraints, functional correctness, factual grounding, architecture consistency, mathematics, security boundaries, missing edge cases, test evidence and output format where observable and relevant. Inspect only artifacts in authorized scope. Use deterministic schema/math checks where objective validation exists; qualify semantic judgments and name missing evidence. A passing build, helper, checklist or model score does not certify the full deliverable.
Do not rerun checks already sufficient for unchanged artifacts or expand a simple edit into a comprehensive review. Report only actionable findings with locations, effect and proportionate correction advice. Preserve the host's requested format and ownership; the host applies fixes and returns the original deliverable. The artifact hook supplies narrow structural feedback separately and is not evidence that these semantic criteria passed.
Output: concise findings, observed verification, unresolved material gaps and any justified next check.''')}


def build():
    metadata={'name':'cognition-os','version':VERSION,'description':'Portable cognitive assistance for agent hosts: 50 mental models, dependency-aware orchestration, evidence checks and governed improvement.','author':{'name':'Cognition OS project'}}
    interface={'displayName':'Cognition OS','shortDescription':'Structured analysis with evidence and validated calculations','longDescription':'Native skills share one catalog of 50 mental models and 52 logical specialist roles. Optional local Python helpers validate calculations and project cases.','developerName':'Cognition OS project','category':'Productivity','defaultPrompt':['Analyze this problem with Cognition OS.','Use Kepner-Tregoe to diagnose this deviation.','Teach me MECE with an infrastructure example.'],'composerIcon':'./assets/icon.svg','logo':'./assets/icon.svg'}
    extension={'interface':interface,'onboardingSkill':'./skills/setup/SKILL.md'}
    write('plugin.json',{'$schema':'https://agent-plugins.org/schemas/1.0.0/plugin.schema.json',**metadata,'extensions':{'com.openai':extension}})
    write('.claude-plugin/plugin.json',metadata)
    # Compatibility fallback only; inline root extension is authoritative on modern OpenAI hosts.
    write('.codex-plugin/plugin.json',{**metadata,'skills':'./skills/','interface':interface,'extensions':{'com.openai':{'onboardingSkill':'./skills/setup/SKILL.md'}}})
    write('assets/icon.svg','<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="128" height="128" viewBox="0 0 128 128"><rect width="128" height="128" rx="26" fill="#142B37"/><g fill="none" stroke="#81D6C4" stroke-width="3"><path d="M64 20 104 44v40l-40 24-40-24V44Z M64 20v88 M24 44l80 40 M104 44 24 84 M24 44h80 M24 84h80"/></g></svg>\n')
    for name,(description,body) in SKILLS.items():
        write(f'skills/{name}/SKILL.md',f'---\nname: {name}\ndescription: {json.dumps(description)}\n---\n\n# {name.replace("-"," ").title()}\n\n{body}\n\nNonactivation: do not apply this skill to unrelated tasks merely because a framework term appears incidentally.\n{COMMON}')
    write('cognitive-core/orchestration/policy.json',{'version':VERSION,'default_mode':'AUTO','modes':{'AUTO':{'frameworks':4,'rebuttal_rounds':1},'QUICK':{'frameworks':2,'rebuttal_rounds':0},'STANDARD':{'frameworks':4,'rebuttal_rounds':1},'DEEP':{'frameworks':8,'rebuttal_rounds':2},'EXECUTIVE':{'frameworks':3,'rebuttal_rounds':1},'CUSTOM':{'frameworks':12,'rebuttal_rounds':2},'LEARN':{'frameworks':1,'rebuttal_rounds':0}},'token_profiles':{'LEAN':{'frameworks':1,'references':1,'context_fraction':0.12},'BALANCED':{'frameworks':4,'references':3,'context_fraction':0.25},'DEEP':{'frameworks':8,'references':6,'context_fraction':0.45}},'default_token_allowance':8000,'budget_kind':'estimate unless host supplies measured usage','parallel_limit':'minimum of host capacity and authorized task limit; no assumed capacity','dependency_policy':'dependent tasks sequential; explicit semantic field mappings','stop_on':['sufficient answer','missing evidence/tool','budget limit','required human judgment'],'further_analysis_condition':'new decision-relevant evidence or unresolved material objection'})
    for name,kind in [('specialist','analytical specialist'),('evaluator','independent evaluator')]:
        body=('Resolve the requested logical AG/FW ID from cognitive-core/agents/registry.json and load only its linked canonical framework. Read references/EXECUTION.md. Execute the distinctive method with cited evidence and UNKNOWN gaps. Return the shared envelope. Do not execute other roles or modify user files unless authorized.' if name=='specialist' else 'Act as AG-52. Read references/REVIEW.md and inspect the supplied artifacts and evidence. Challenge unsupported facts, assumptions, contradictions and calculations. Return ACCEPT, CONDITIONAL, REJECT or INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE with observable justification and unresolved objections. Never require consensus or fabricate confidence.')
        write(f'agents/cognition-{name}.md',f'---\nname: cognition-{name}\ndescription: Cognition OS {kind} for explicitly delegated structured analysis and evidence review.\ntools: Read, Glob, Grep\n---\n\nResolve packaged paths from this installed plugin root.\n\n{body}\n')
    write('.agents/plugins/marketplace.json',{'name':'cognition-os-local','interface':{'displayName':'Cognition OS local development'},'plugins':[{'name':'cognition-os','source':{'source':'local','path':'./local-marketplace/plugins/cognition-os'},'policy':{'installation':'AVAILABLE','authentication':'ON_INSTALL'},'category':'Productivity'}]})
    write('.claude-plugin/marketplace.json',{'name':'cognition-os-local','owner':{'name':'Cognition OS project'},'metadata':{'description':'Private local Cognition OS development catalog'},'plugins':[{'name':'cognition-os','source':'./','description':metadata['description'],'version':VERSION}]})
    write('docs/SKILL_SPECIFICATIONS.md','# Native skill boundaries — V4.1\n\n'+ '\n'.join(f'- **{n}**: {d}' for n,(d,b) in SKILLS.items())+f'\n\n{len(SKILLS)} focused entrypoints share the canonical core. Model-selected assistance is primary; setup and manual invocation are optional diagnostics. No skill is exposed per individual framework. Each entrypoint defines scope, method, nonactivation, internal output, recovery and permissions. The host retains task and deliverable ownership.\n')
    build_schemas()
    from build_hybrid import build as build_hybrid
    build_hybrid()
    print(f'Generated {len(SKILLS)} skills, two native Claude agent wrappers and three manifests.')

def build_schemas():
    base={'$schema':'https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema'}
    def obj(required,properties):return {'type':'object','required':required,'properties':properties,'additionalProperties':False}
    text={'type':'string','minLength':1}; array={'type':'array','items':text}; anyobj={'type':'object'}
    claim_types=['VERIFIED_FACT','SOURCE_SUPPORTED','CALCULATED_RESULT','SIMULATED_RESULT','USER_ASSUMPTION','MODEL_INFERENCE','HYPOTHESIS','UNKNOWN']
    schemas={
      'framework':obj(['id','agent_id','name','category','required_inputs','methodology','expected_outputs','source'],{k:v for k,v in []}),
      'agent-envelope':obj(['envelope_version','session_id','trace_id','agent_id','framework_id','execution_kind','status','upstream_entity_ids','inputs','payload','claims','gaps'],{
        'envelope_version':{'const':'3.1'},'session_id':text,'trace_id':text,'agent_id':{'type':'string','pattern':'^AG-(0[1-9]|[1-4][0-9]|5[0-2])$'},'framework_id':{'type':['string','null'],'pattern':'^FW-(0[1-9]|[1-4][0-9]|50)$'},
        'execution_kind':{'enum':['SEQUENTIAL_HOST_ROLE','NATIVE_SUBAGENT','DETERMINISTIC_TOOL']},'status':{'enum':['COMPLETED','PARTIAL','BLOCKED','FAILED']},'upstream_entity_ids':array,'inputs':anyobj,'payload':anyobj,
        'claims':{'type':'array','items':obj(['id','text','classification','evidence_ids'],{'id':text,'text':text,'classification':{'enum':claim_types},'evidence_ids':array,'material':{'type':'boolean'}})},'gaps':array,'tool_execution_ids':array}),
      'evidence':obj(['id','kind','locator','content'],{'id':text,'kind':{'enum':['source','assumption','calculation','simulation','observation']},'locator':text,'content':text,'retrieved_at':text,'method':text,'inputs':{},'result':{},'verification':obj(['status','checked_at'],{'status':{'enum':['VERIFIED','UNVERIFIED']},'checked_at':text})}),
      'decision':obj(['id','recommendation','verdict','claims','alternatives','risks','conditions','human_decision'],{'id':text,'recommendation':text,'verdict':{'enum':['ACCEPT','CONDITIONAL','REJECT','INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE']},'claims':{'type':'array','items':anyobj},'alternatives':array,'risks':array,'conditions':array,'human_decision':{'enum':['PENDING','APPROVED','REJECTED','NOT_REQUESTED']}}),
      'provenance':obj(['nodes','edges'],{'nodes':{'type':'array','items':obj(['id','kind'],{'id':text,'kind':{'enum':['Entity','Activity','Agent']},'label':text})},'edges':{'type':'array','items':obj(['source','target','relation'],{'source':text,'target':text,'relation':{'enum':['used','wasGeneratedBy','wasDerivedFrom','wasAssociatedWith','wasAttributedTo']}})} }),
      'agent':{'type':'object','required':['id','name','kind','framework_id','source','responsibilities'],'properties':{'id':{'type':'string','pattern':'^AG-(0[1-9]|[1-4][0-9]|5[0-2])$'},'name':text,'kind':text,'framework_id':{'type':['string','null']},'source':anyobj,'responsibilities':array,'execution':text,'contract':text},'additionalProperties':False}
    }
    sample=json.loads((ROOT/'cognitive-core/frameworks/definitions/FW-01.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
    schemas['framework']['properties']={k:({'type':'array','items':text} if isinstance(v,list) and (not v or isinstance(v[0],str)) else {'type':'array','items':anyobj} if isinstance(v,list) else anyobj if isinstance(v,dict) else text) for k,v in sample.items()}
    schemas['framework']['properties']['id']={'type':'string','pattern':'^FW-(0[1-9]|[1-4][0-9]|50)$'}
    for name,schema in schemas.items():write(f'schemas/{name}.schema.json',base|schema)
    # Tighten analytical payloads. Explicit UNKNOWN gaps are represented by an object.
    string_fields={'recommendation','conclusion','question','situation','complication','answer','governing_thought','constraint','domain','response_protocol','archetype','effect_type','hmw','contradiction','feedback_script','claim','warrant','backing','qualifier','rebuttal'}
    number_fields={'gross_ev','net_ev','posterior','bayes_factor','bcr','npv','break_even'}
    for p in (ROOT/'schemas/framework-output').glob('*.json'):
        s=json.loads(p.read_text())
        for field in s['properties']:
            s['properties'][field]={'type':['number','object','null']} if field in number_fields else {'type':['string','object']} if field in string_fields else {'type':['array','object']}
        write(p.relative_to(ROOT),s)
    write('schemas/framework-output/FW-11.schema.json',base|obj(['is_vs_is_not_matrix','candidate_causes','diagnostic_tests','conclusion'],{
        'is_vs_is_not_matrix':obj(['what','where','when','extent'],{dim:obj(['is','is_not','distinction','change'],{k:text for k in ['is','is_not','distinction','change']}) for dim in ['what','where','when','extent']}),
        'candidate_causes':{'type':'array','items':obj(['cause','fits_is','fits_is_not','status','evidence_ids'],{'cause':text,'fits_is':text,'fits_is_not':text,'status':{'enum':['HYPOTHESIS','REJECTED','SUPPORTED','VERIFIED']},'evidence_ids':array})},
        'diagnostic_tests':{'type':'array','minItems':1,'items':obj(['test','falsifies','required_evidence'],{'test':text,'falsifies':text,'required_evidence':array})},'conclusion':text}))

if __name__=='__main__':build()
